\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. We sing the praise of Him who died,
\par Of Him who died upon the Cross:
\par The sinners hope led deride: 
\par For this we count the world but loss.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2 Inscribed upon the Cross we see
\par In shining letters: God is love.
\par He bears our sins upon t5he tree:
\par He brings us mercy from above.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3 The Cross-it takes our guilt away:
\par It5 holds the fainting spirit up; 
\par It cheers with hope the gloomy day,
\par And sweetens ever bitter cup.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4 It makes the coward spirit brave,
\par And nerves the feeble arm for fight;
\par It takes it s terror from the grave,
\par And gilds the bed of death with light.
\par  
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5 The balm of life, the cure of woe,
\par The measure and the pledge of love.
\par The sinner's refuge here below,
\par The angels' theme in Heaven above.
\par 
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

